/* worksheets-ink: the module's own test. run_checks.sh runs it when the course
 * switches the module on (build.py --list-checks).
 *
 * On the course's own data: the page carries the module, working; every document's
 * worksheet holds one problem, with its number, for each question the document's
 * plan puts on it, and its solutions one answer per problem, with nothing undefined.
 * The build step: an item naming a question the bank does not have, a document of an
 * unknown type, a problem set CHAINS does not have, a question on two documents, a
 * SOURCE_OF that disagrees with the items and an option holding a lookbehind each stop
 * the build with that reason.
 * On a scratch copy with eight of Basic-Pharmacokinetics' documents (Quiz 1, Homework 2,
 * daily practice 2 and 3 of Module 1, the worked examples of Module 6a, the in-class
 * activities of Modules 7a and 7b, the worked examples of Module 8), their 61 questions
 * (with the questions their dupOf names), 12 problem sets, 7 topics, 13 skills and 5 lectures, verbatim from
 * ac2eb73 (src/sources.js, the q files, course.js; ids prefixed wsi-; the professor is
 * Basic-Pharmacokinetics' own, added to COURSE.professors), and Basic-Pharmacokinetics' options: the plan of each worksheet and who solved each part are those of
 * Basic-Pharmacokinetics' own sheetPlan and solvedBy (src/views.js, at ac2eb73,
 * recorded below as EXPECT). Then src/ink_test.py, ported to Node Playwright, in
 * Chromium at 820 px and 390 px: the work areas, More room and Less room, a stroke
 * drawn with the mouse kept on its problem and drawn on its canvas, undo, redo, the
 * eraser, a colour returning to the pen, the name line, a pen that switches to Pencil
 * only and then a finger that scrolls, Show solutions, no sideways scroll, Save as PDF
 * with the ink as pictures (in the print layout: the paper laid out, every problem with
 * its text, the ink's picture over its problem holding the stroke, the paper rendered in
 * print media; and, in Chromium only, the PDF's size, since page.pdf is Chromium's
 * only: in WebKit that line says NOT RUN), Done, the writing and room back after a reload, Clear page
 * and its undo; Scratch paper in the quiz and on an exam paper (stem over 720 px, no
 * solutions, the paper's clock, the old paper's scratch cleared); Hold to snap (line,
 * its end following the pen, ellipse, box, scribble, switch off and its saved choice,
 * highlighter straightening only and under the writing), two fingers tapped together
 * undo, a scroll, a cancelled touch and a resting hand undo nothing, the eraser on a
 * snapped line's middle, no selection or menu. Pen and touch input are synthetic
 * PointerEvents and mouse strokes from Playwright, in Chromium only: no Apple Pencil,
 * iPad or Safari ran.
 * What this kit adds over the course's test: the writing is kept in the profile's
 * progress (DB.ink) and in no localStorage key of its own; Import progress brings it
 * back, a second profile has none, Erase my history removes it, the Settings section
 * says how much is kept and erases it keeping the answers; the size of a stroke and of
 * the progress is printed; Practice in the drill asks the sheet's problems in its order.
 * Practice in the drill with chained-problem-sets off (one pass in the sheet's order) and on (a sheet that is
 * one whole problem set starts that set), the second when the course carries that module.
 * Persistence, with much writing (61 pages, 1801 strokes): saved whole and back after a reload; Export
 * progress holds it and Import brings it back into a fresh profile; each profile keeps its own after a switch;
 * a stroke survives a reload at once and after 300 ms (the core's own 150 ms wait for an answer is reported);
 * storage denied (setItem throws) and storage full (this browser's own localStorage quota, filled with
 * writing): the page says on screen that the writing was not saved, nothing saved before is overwritten, an
 * answer given after a refused stroke is still saved, and after a reload, or once Erase all writing makes
 * room, the answers and the writing saved before load and new writing is saved.
 * The core's save path (kit PR #17, F1, 2026-11-06): ink is written through the core's save() and saveNow(), so
 * after ink an answer, a second stroke, a flag (a module's own part, as study-controls keeps it) and a setting on
 * the same page are stored with no stale-page wall, and survive a reload, also after ink on an exam paper's
 * Scratch paper; two tabs of one profile, without Web Locks (tab B saves, then a stroke in tab A: A shows the
 * stale-page wall and writes nothing over B) and with them (B opens read-only, takes the profile with Use it
 * here and saves; a stroke in A writes nothing over B); ink stored before the change (DB.ink in the progress)
 * opens with the answers, a flag and a setting and is kept beside new writing; with storage full the core's
 * notice, which is allowed there, must say the progress is saved, and with storage denied that it is not.
 * The independent review of 0769d14: with this tab's writes refused and then another tab's save, the next stroke
 * is 'stopped' (the wall), not 'off'; a stroke held while the profile's lock is being given (WRITER 'pending', set
 * by the test) is written once the page has it, and a refused stroke after it puts back the writing stored, not
 * older writing; with storage denied a stroke not saved is in this visit's copy of the progress and stays after a
 * profile switch and back; Save as PDF opens the print dialog only after every ink picture is decoded.
 *
 *     node features/worksheets-ink/test.js
 */
const fs = require('fs'), path = require('path');
const L = require(path.join(__dirname, '..', '..', 'check_lib'));
const NAME = 'features/worksheets-ink/test.js';
const {check} = L;
